{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012HiRtNHvfgWcpqAsZ6NTnN","type":"tool_result","content":"/bin/bash: line 1: cd: engine: No such file or directory\n9:## Quick start (a complete game)\n40:## Look target (read this before drawing anything)\n53:## Coordinates: what x, y, z mean in each view\n69:## Rules\n78:## Common mistakes (check these first)\n86:## Game\n102:## Scenes (title, play, game over)\n113:## Motion and timing: tweens, scripts, paths, weather\n129:## Standard features (every game has them: don't build your own)\n136:## Input: `game.input`\n143:- Controller settings: `deadzone` (default `.18`, radial and rescaled), `invertAimY`, `lastDevice` (the index has the rest). The left stick and the touch stick, pushed past halfway, press `up` / `down` / `left` / `right` as the d-pad does (menus, dialog choices, ladders); bind `PadAxisUp/Down/Left/Right` to your own menu actions for the same.\n146:## Drawing: `r` in `draw(r)`\n155:## Pixels, sprites, text, UI\n158:- Font (5x7 proportional with lower case; `font: 'tiny'` for 3x5): `E.font.text(g, str, x, y, color, { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font })`, `E.font.title(g, str, x, y, { scale, colors, outline, depth, depthColor, align })`, `E.font.width(str, opts)`, `E.font.lineHeight(opts)`, `E.font.wrap(str, maxW, opts)`. Glyphs: ASCII plus `♥ ★ ← → ↑ ↓ • × ♪ ▸ ©`.\n164:## Sound: `game.audio` (chip synth, no files, starts after the first key press)\n170:## Levels\n182:## Movement and physics\n200:## Characters\n216:## Effects and lighting\n222:## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\n234:| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\n235:| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\n262:## More: animation and examples outside this card\n286:## Before you hand the game back","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df25608b-8d30-41bd-8640-efa7a82527f1","uuid":"488d28e0-0451-43b6-b092-52d3bc4dabf7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:30:38.460Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/bin/bash: line 1: cd: engine: No such file or directory\n9:## Quick start (a complete game)\n40:## Look target (read this before drawing anything)\n53:## Coordinates: what x, y, z mean in each view\n69:## Rules\n78:## Common mistakes (check these first)\n86:## Game\n102:## Scenes (title, play, game over)\n113:## Motion and timing: tweens, scripts, paths, weather\n129:## Standard features (every game has them: don't build your own)\n136:## Input: `game.input`\n143:- Controller settings: `deadzone` (default `.18`, radial and rescaled), `invertAimY`, `lastDevice` (the index has the rest). The left stick and the touch stick, pushed past halfway, press `up` / `down` / `left` / `right` as the d-pad does (menus, dialog choices, ladders); bind `PadAxisUp/Down/Left/Right` to your own menu actions for the same.\n146:## Drawing: `r` in `draw(r)`\n155:## Pixels, sprites, text, UI\n158:- Font (5x7 proportional with lower case; `font: 'tiny'` for 3x5): `E.font.text(g, str, x, y, color, { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font })`, `E.font.title(g, str, x, y, { scale, colors, outline, depth, depthColor, align })`, `E.font.width(str, opts)`, `E.font.lineHeight(opts)`, `E.font.wrap(str, maxW, opts)`. Glyphs: ASCII plus `♥ ★ ← → ↑ ↓ • × ♪ ▸ ©`.\n164:## Sound: `game.audio` (chip synth, no files, starts after the first key press)\n170:## Levels\n182:## Movement and physics\n200:## Characters\n216:## Effects and lighting\n222:## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\n234:| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\n235:| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\n262:## More: animation and examples outside this card\n286:## Before you hand the game back","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012HiRtNHvfgWcpqAsZ6NTnN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
