{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018tWuqG1gqaD2vfDYmcrrTh","type":"tool_result","content":"28:Testing: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state (the engine’s game.advance and game.debug, as in game/test.mjs), including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n42:Attract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df25608b-8d30-41bd-8640-efa7a82527f1","uuid":"6e5b2157-4a8a-473c-b9c9-65f216790f3a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:12:51.814Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"28:Testing: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state (the engine’s game.advance and game.debug, as in game/test.mjs), including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n42:Attract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the a