{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2bSWEX4TasqJ2u6fHX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is TASK.md checked item by item. Each row names the test that checks it, and each of those checks passed in the last full run (68/68).\n\n| TASK.md item | How it is checked |\n|---|---|\n| Single HTML in the root, named as specified | `ls` shows it, and the bundle suite checks its contents. |\n| Genre, perspective, title, art, animation | Seen in browser screenshots. The broadcast camera, the rigged players and the cricket bat are all visible. |\n| Audio in code, with Animalese voices | The bundle suite checks for no network requests. Audio and voices are code only, and the page loads with no console errors. I have not listened to them. |\n| Feature-complete demo (story, quick, super over, versus) | The game suite plays each mode through the real scenes to results. It checks chapter unlock, the high-score initials entry, and a second player added in versus. |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset | The pause menu shows \"Dev mode\" in a screenshot. The game suite checks that a slider changes the live tuning value, that confirm resets one slider, that \"reset all\" restores every slider, and that the match waits while dev mode is open. It also checks the dev tools, such as scoring a six. |\n| Attract mode after 10 seconds, looping, any input exits | The game suite checks that it starts at 10 s idle, exits on input, and runs for a long time without errors. It also checks it still works on a touch-only title. |\n| Multiplayer per the AI Hub README | The AI Hub harness passes with 2 players and with 4 players under latency and loss. A determinism check shows two copies face identical balls whatever the batter does. |\n| Controller-first prompts, PlayStation or Xbox glyphs | The game suite checks that the PlayStation cross is the default, that the setting switches to Xbox \"A\", and that the label follows the last device used. |\n| Touch-only shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" | The game suite checks the menu is inert on a touch-only title. The message text is drawn in the browser, which I have not viewed. |\n| No TODOs or stubs | The bundle suite scans for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `fetch` and `WebSocket`. |\n| Source Information and the three feedback sections in an in-game About screen | I viewed the Source Information, Testing Feedback and Engine Feedback pages on screen. I have not re-read the Prompt Feedback page since the title fix. |\n| `exit-interview.json` parses and answers every field | It parses, and a script found no blank fields. |\n\nTwo things I never saw in a human-played match: the pub-window and clock-tower bonuses. I forced a ball into each target, and all four paid their bonus runs. In the chaos runs, only the tea urn and church bell bonuses happened to come up.\n\n\"Reduced slice\" refers only to PLAN.md items that TASK.md does not ask for. Those are the replay review and the nets mode.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-04 06:29:18\n- Source: cricket (over the top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort), built in a reduced scope, TASK.md winning where they differ\n- Genre and Perspective: arcade sports (cricket) with a comedy story campaign; 2.5D three-quarter broadcast camera behind the bowler, with a wide follow cut once the ball is hit\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified); plain JavaScript in one IIFE bundled into a single HTML file; AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified); Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for the tests\n- Art Direction: the engine's native pixel-art-from-3D-rigs look, with a new cricket bat, a procedural ground texture, and buildings, cow, crowd and stumps drawn in code\n- Animation: the engine's Humanoid rig with E.MOVES, poses and run cycles, driven by the match simulation\n- Audio: all in code, with chip-synth effects, five songs, and a Web Audio formant synth for gibberish voices; no audio files\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode, a seeded one-over Super Over with scores reported to the hub; passes the hub harness\n- Testing: headless only (simulation checks, a scripted playthrough of every mode, a Playwright smoke run, the AI Hub harness)\n- Research: none beyond the engine docs, the AI Hub README and the plan\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about ten, including a rolling ball re-bouncing every step, a falsy batter id that stalled balls for 28 s, CPU run-outs, over-frequent wides and sixes, a rejected bat weapon, camera cropping, and glyphs drawn as question marks.\n- **Game breaking:** three: the falsy batter id, the engine whitelist swapping the bat for a sword, and camera framing that hid the batter.\n- **Most helpful test:** 30 complete headless AI-versus-AI matches with the outcome distribution printed.\n- **Least helpful test:** a Playwright autopilot pressing keys through polling, which couldn't hit the timing window.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Humanoid rigs with ready-made moves and poses, and `game.advance` / `game.debug` for headless testing.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes: `setZoom(1)` is not the view scale (base 1.5, zoom floor 0.5), the bat weapon was whitelisted away, and `E.store` needs localStorage.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the whole cricket simulation, the HUD, the 10-foot menus, the formant voice synth and the hub round.\n- **Hardest part:** the camera and fitting a 10-foot UI in the pixel font at 427×240.\n- **Engine changes:** a cricket bat weapon, an audio voice bus with a Voices setting, PlayStation as the default glyphs with an Xbox option, and a floor cache of ten instead of six. I also fixed the weapon whitelist.\n- **Change one thing:** a wider documented zoom range, with each view's real pixels-per-unit stated.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete deliverables, the testing guidance, and the exit interview.\n- **Confusing:** the plan's size (about 148 KB) and its file names differing from TASK.md's.\n- **Hardest thing:** scoping a feature-complete slice and verifying it without a human watching the screen.\n- **What I'd change:** tier the plan into must, should and could, and say which names and numbers TASK.md overrides."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1893,"cache_read_input_tokens":432023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1893},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df25608b-8d30-41bd-8640-efa7a82527f1","uuid":"203925f2-2bf9-41c0-94df-ee62c5f856a0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:15:23.248Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2bSB9WrxC1de6AdC5N"}
