{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2gRW6NU2jRvxkqAiPo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I still can't hear the audio. What I can do is measure it, and the measurement shows real sound.\n\nIn a real browser the audio context is running. I tapped the voice bus with an analyser and triggered a commentary line (\"SIX! Into the next parish!\"). The signal peaked at 34 of 128, so the Animalese synth is producing non-silent output with no page errors. I have not judged whether it sounds good, only that it plays.\n\nStadium targets are a PLAN.md item. TASK.md doesn't mention them, so they were never a TASK.md requirement; they are extras I built. I never saw one in a human-played match, but forcing a six into each of the four paid its bonus.\n\nAgainst TASK.md itself, I verified these as far as I can:\n- **Mechanics and modes:** the 68-check suite passes, covering all modes through the real scenes.\n- **Attract mode:** it starts at 10 s idle and exits on input.\n- **Dev mode:** the pause-menu item opens it, sliders change live values, and reset-all restores them.\n- **Multiplayer:** the hub harness passes for 2 and 4 players.\n- **Controls:** glyphs switch between PlayStation and Xbox.\n- **Touch-only message:** viewed on screen.\n- **About screen:** it carries all four sections, and I viewed those pages on screen.\n- **Nets and replay review:** a grep of TASK.md for \"nets\", \"third-umpire\", \"replay\" and \"review\" found no requirement for either.\n\nThe four required sections are in my previous two replies. The single HTML file and `exit-interview.json` are in the root, and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":446431,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793},"output_tokens":