{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2gtP7meMCG22uu4WJZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All of the work is done; the only gap that remains is the sound quality, which I can't judge. Here are the four sections in this message, as the condition wants.\n\nTASK.md doesn't ask for Nets, a replay review or stadium targets. I grepped it for \"nets\", \"third-umpire\", \"replay\" and \"review\", and the only hits were the testing line \"don't use subagents to … review\" and the attract-mode \"scripted replay\" wording, which my AI-played attract mode meets. The stadium targets are an extra I built, not a TASK.md requirement.\n\nThe audio and Animalese voices play and are measurably non-silent: a running audio context, and an analyser peak of 34 of 128 on the voice bus in a real browser. I have not judged how they sound, which I can't do.\n\nThe single HTML is in the root, `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled, and the last full test run was 68/68.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-04 06:29:18\n- Source: cricket (over the top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort), built in a reduced scope, TASK.md winning where they differ\n- Genre and Perspective: arcade sports (cricket) with a comedy story campaign; 2.5D three-quarter broadcast camera behind the bowler, with a wide follow cut once the ball is hit\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified); plain JavaScript in one IIFE bundled into a single HTML file; AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified); Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for the tests\n- Art Direction: the engine's native pixel-art-from-3D-rigs look, with a new cricket bat, a procedural ground texture, and buildings, cow, crowd and stumps drawn in code\n- Animation: the engine's Humanoid rig with E.MOVES, poses and run cycles, driven by the match simulation\n- Audio: all in code, with chip-synth effects, five songs, and a Web Audio formant synth for gibberish voices; no audio files\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode, a seeded one-over Super Over with scores reported to the hub; passes the hub harness\n- Testing: headless only (simulation checks, a scripted playthrough of every mode, a Playwright smoke run, the AI Hub harness)\n- Research: none beyond the engine docs, the AI Hub README and the plan\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about ten, including a rolling ball re-bouncing every step, a falsy batter id that stalled balls for 28 s, CPU run-outs, over-frequent wides and sixes, a rejected bat weapon, camera cropping, and glyphs drawn as question marks.\n- **Game breaking:** three: the falsy batter id, the engine whitelist swapping the bat for a sword, and camera framing that hid the batter.\n- **Most helpful test:** 30 complete headless AI-versus-AI matches with the outcome distribution printed.\n- **Least helpful test:** a Playwright autopilot pressing keys through polling, which couldn't hit the timing window.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Humanoid rigs with ready-made moves and poses, and `game.advance` / `game.debug` for headless testing.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes: `setZoom(1)` is not the view scale (base 1.5, zoom floor 0.5), the bat weapon was whitelisted away, and `E.store` needs localStorage.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the whole cricket simulation, the HUD, the 10-foot menus, the formant voice synth and the hub round.\n- **Hardest part:** the camera and fitting a 10-foot UI in the pixel font at 427×240.\n- **Engine changes:** a cricket bat weapon, an audio voice bus with a Voices setting, PlayStation as the default glyphs with an Xbox option, and a floor cache of ten instead of six. I also fixed the weapon whitelist.\n- **Change one thing:** a wider documented zoom range, with each view's real pixels-per-unit stated.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete deliverables, the testing guidance, and the exit interview.\n- **Confusing:** the plan's size (about 148 KB) and its file names differing from TASK.md's.\n- **Hardest thing:** scoping a feature-complete slice and verifying it without a human watching the screen.\n- **What I'd change:** tier the plan into must, should and could, and say which names and numbers TASK.md overrides."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":447224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df25608b-8d30-41bd-8640-efa7a82527f1","uuid":"e38c6a38-0c39-4e8e-a65e-d104cf2fec78","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:16:30.837Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2gt1JPTxVgH9GYVFiM"}
