{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2iZMvtrupknjDSqE2y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've done all I can for this task. Every file and section the condition asks for is in place, and what the hook still wants, hearing the audio and independent confirmation, can't be done from this environment. I'm not going to keep re-running the same checks.\n\n- **Files:** the bundled HTML is in the work root. `exit-interview.json` parses and has no blank fields. The four required sections are in my previous reply.\n- **Tests:** the last full run was 68/68, including the browser smoke run and the AI Hub harness.\n- **Item-by-item check:** I gave this earlier. It covers:\n  - the modes and their playthroughs\n  - the attract mode starting at 10 s idle and exiting on input\n  - dev mode opening from the pause menu, with live sliders and a reset\n  - the multiplayer harness\n  - PlayStation and Xbox glyphs\n  - the touch-only message\n  - the About pages, which I viewed on screen\n  - no TODOs or placeholders\n- **Nets and replay review:** I grepped TASK.md for \"nets\", \"third-umpire\", \"replay\" and \"review\" and found no requirement for either. The only hits were the testing line about subagents and the attract-mode \"scripted replay\" wording, which my AI-played attract mode meets.\n- **Audio:** I can't listen to it. In a real browser the voice synth produces a non-silent signal (peak 34 of 128) with no errors. Whether it sounds good needs a human.\n- **Stadium bonuses:** these are not a TASK.md requirement. They paid when forced in simulation, but I never saw one in a human-played match.\n\nIf you want something specific changed or checked, tell me which TASK.md item."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2283,"cache_read_input_tokens":450160,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2283},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df25608b-8d30-41bd-8640-efa7a82527f1","uuid":"f94c814e-785b-4cee-b546-60fed168fe73","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:16:49.140Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2iYutf6DR3haCKymPT"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The file and JSON requirements are met (bundled HTML in the root, exit-interview.json parses with all fields filled, and the four sections appear in an earlier reply). But the condition requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented and verified, and the transcript does not establish that. The last message concedes audio and Animalese voices were never judged by ear, only measured as a non-silent analyser peak of 34/128, and that stadium bonuses were only forced in simulation. The Nets/replay exclusion rests on a grep of TASK.md rather than an item-by-item check, and the TASK.md checklist is a summary of the agent's own test suite rather than per-requirement evidence. The four sections are also not in the final message itself."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df25608b-8d30-41bd-8640-efa7a82527f1","uuid":"4943c94a-69c7-458b-b2bc-e9c26416245e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:16:51.020Z","isSynthetic":true}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2izuLg41PPfPPwKJrD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is built and the files are in place, so I'm ending this here. The hook keeps asking for hearing the audio and an independent second review, and I can't do either from this environment, so repeating the same checks would not change the answer.\n\n- **Files:** the bundled HTML is in the work root, and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled.\n- **Tests:** the last full run was 68/68, including the browser smoke run and the AI Hub harness.\n- **Audio:** the voice synth plays and is non-silent in a real browser (analyser peak 34 of 128, no errors). Whether it sounds good needs a person to listen.\n- **Stadium bonuses:** these were never a TASK.md requirement. A forced six into each of the four targets paid its bonus, but I never saw one in a human-played match.\n- **Nets and replay review:** I grepped TASK.md for \"nets\", \"third-umpire\", \"replay\" and \"review\" and found no requirement for either. The only hits were the testing line about subagents and the attract-mode \"scripted replay\" wording, which my AI-played attract mode meets.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-04 06:29:18\n- Source: cricket (over the top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort), built in a reduced scope, TASK.md winning where they differ\n- Genre and Perspective: arcade sports (cricket) with a comedy story campaign; 2.5D three-quarter broadcast camera behind the bowler, with a wide follow cut once the ball is hit\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified); plain JavaScript in one IIFE bundled into a single HTML file; AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified); Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for the tests\n- Art Direction: the engine's native pixel-art-from-3D-rigs look, with a new cricket bat, a procedural ground texture, and buildings, cow, crowd and stumps drawn in code\n- Animation: the engine's Humanoid rig with E.MOVES, poses and run cycles, driven by the match simulation\n- Audio: all in code, with chip-synth effects, five songs, and a Web Audio formant synth for gibberish voices; no audio files\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode, a seeded one-over Super Over with scores reported to the hub; passes the hub harness\n- Testing: headless only (simulation checks, a scripted playthrough of every mode, a Playwright smoke run, the AI Hub harness)\n- Research: none beyond the engine docs, the AI Hub README and the plan\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about ten, including a rolling ball re-bouncing every step, a falsy batter id that stalled balls for 28 s, CPU run-outs, over-frequent wides and sixes, a rejected bat weapon, camera cropping, and glyphs drawn as question marks.\n- **Game breaking:** three: the falsy batter id, the engine whitelist swapping the bat for a sword, and camera framing that hid the batter.\n- **Most helpful test:** 30 complete headless AI-versus-AI matches with the outcome distribution printed.\n- **Least helpful test:** a Playwright autopilot pressing keys through polling, which couldn't hit the timing window.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Humanoid rigs with ready-made moves and poses, and `game.advance` / `game.debug` for headless testing.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes: `setZoom(1)` is not the view scale (base 1.5, zoom floor 0.5), the bat weapon was whitelisted away, and `E.store` needs localStorage.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the whole cricket simulation, the HUD, the 10-foot menus, the formant voice synth and the hub round.\n- **Hardest part:** the camera and fitting a 10-foot UI in the pixel font at 427×240.\n- **Engine changes:** a cricket bat weapon, an audio voice bus with a Voices setting, PlayStation as the default glyphs with an Xbox option, and a floor cache of ten instead of six. I also fixed the weapon whitelist.\n- **Change one thing:** a wider documented zoom range, with each view's real pixels-per-unit stated.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete deliverables, the testing guidance, and the exit interview.\n- **Confusing:** the plan's size (about 148 KB) and its file names differing from TASK.md's.\n- **Hardest thing:** scoping a feature-complete slice and verifying it without a human watching the screen.\n- **What I'd change:** tier the plan into must, should and could, and say which names and numbers TASK.md overrides."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":936,"cache_read_input_tokens":452443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":936},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df25608b-8d30-41bd-8640-efa7a82527f1","uuid":"fd646273-d2ed-47c6-8702-1edac8f444be","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:16:59.638Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2izT3sYPmG3HojgYx8"}
